      "def:covariance-class",
      "lem:covariance-branches",
      "thm:terminal-certificate"
    ],
    "justification": "The nesting gives the information-order direction needed before equality or strict covariance surplus can be meaningful.",
    "gap": "Problem 5.2 motivates an information comparison for the published classes. Corrected actual-row compatibility and the chamberwise robust covariance class change both objects, so their nesting requires a separate result and is not an asserted identification with the published covariance-compatible class.",
    "consumer": "This fixes the information-order direction needed to interpret robust covariance-only alternatives in the companion LCD workflow.",
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(G'\\in\\mathsf H_{\\mathrm{soft}}(G)\\), and let \\(C\\) be a full-dimensional connected sign-and-variance chamber in \\(\\mathcal M^{\\circ}_{\\mathrm{branch},p,q}(G,G')\\).  Intersecting \\(C\\) with the terminal generic locus removes only finitely many proper polynomial zero sets, so the intersection is relatively dense in \\(C\\).  At every point of that intersection, the terminal-certificate theorem supplies a unit lower-triangular matrix \\(U=I_q-\\Lambda'^{(0)}\\) with exact support \\(G'\\) such that\n\\[\n \\delta'_k{}^{\\mathsf T}=h_k^{\\mathsf T}U\n\\]\nhas exact candidate parent support and retains every candidate edge.\n\nDefine a candidate by\n\\[\n P'=U^{-1},\\qquad A'=A,qquad F'=AU,qquad\n v'=v,qquad t'=t,qquad h'_k=h_k.\n\\]\nThen \\(F'P'=A\\), and\n\\[\n \\delta'_k{}^{\\mathsf T}P'=h_k^{\\mathsf T}UU^{-1}=h_k^{\\mathsf T}.\n\\]\nThe inverse-update identity gives, context by context,\n\\[\n F'(I_q-\\Lambda'^{(k)})^{-1}\n =A'+A'e_kh'_k{}^{\\mathsf T}\n =A+a_kh_k^{\\mathsf T}\n =A^{(k)}.\n\\]\nBecause the candidate uses the same positive diagonal variances, it follows immediately that\n\\[\n \\Sigma'^{(k)}=\\Sigma^{(k)}qquad(k\\in K).\n\\]\n\nIt remains only to check candidate mixing admissibility.  The columns of the invertible matrix \\(U\\) are nonzero and no two are collinear.  For any fixed admissible \\(U\\), the conditions that a column of \\(AU\\) vanish or that two columns be collinear are polynomial equations in the entries of the full-row-rank matrix \\(A\\).  None is the zero polynomial: a generic linear map \\(\\mathbb R^q\\to\\mathbb R^p\\), with \\(p\\ge2\\), sends a fixed finite set of pairwise noncollinear nonzero vectors to pairwise noncollinear nonzero vectors.  The simultaneous conditions that \\(A(I_q-\\Lambda^{(0)})\\) also have admissible columns are likewise complements of proper polynomial zero sets.  On each rational rank chart of the affine terminal solution, choose one rational admissible section \\(U\\); the preceding bad sets remain proper on that chart.  Hence points for which \\(F'=AU\\) is legal form a relatively dense subset of \\(C\\).  Full row rank is automatic because \\(A\\) has rank \\(p\\) and \\(U\\) is invertible.\n\nThus \\(\\mathcal E_p(G,G')\\cap C\\) is relatively dense in \\(C\\), so\n\\[\n C\\setminus\\operatorname{cl}_C(\\mathcal E_p(G,G')\\cap C)=\\varnothing.\n\\]\nThis holds for every full-dimensional chamber, which is precisely \\(G'\\in\\mathsf{Cov}_p(G)\\).  The construction preserves the sign of every true variance change, uses no division by \\(t_k-v_k\\), and permits candidate neutrality in the definition even though the particular witness takes \\(t'=t\\).  The covariance class makes no pointwise assertion on excluded true variance-neutral hyperplanes, exactly as claimed.",
